From: GitHub Copilot <copilot@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: build ffmpeg with PIC for shared plugin linking

FFmpeg 8.1's x86_64 nasm objects (notably libavutil's av_tx transform,
tx_float.o) emit non-PIC relocations. Linking the static libavutil into a
VLC shared plugin that uses the FFT -- stream_out_chromaprint auto-selects
the avtx backend -- then fails the shared link:

  relocation R_X86_64_PC32 against symbol `ff_tx_tab_32_float' can not be
  used when making a shared object; recompile with -fPIC

Enable ffmpeg's --enable-pic so its assembly is position-independent and can
be linked into VLC's shared plugins. This is a no-op where the asm is already
position-independent (arm/arm64) and fixes the x86_64 shared-plugin link.
---
 contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak b/contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak
--- a/contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 # bsf=vp9_superframe is needed to mux VP9 inside webm/mkv
-FFMPEGCONF = --prefix="$(PREFIX)" --enable-static --disable-shared \
+FFMPEGCONF = --prefix="$(PREFIX)" --enable-static --disable-shared --enable-pic \
 	--extra-ldflags="$(LDFLAGS)" \
 	--cc="$(CC)" \
